  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_3' aria-label=\" Shuvendu Saha versus The State of West Bengal and Anr. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('3','2026','2026_5_221_237','2026INSC367'); ><font size='4'> <strong>SHUVENDU SAHA<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>THE STATE OF WEST BENGAL AND ANR. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 5 S.C.R. 221</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 367</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001442026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : VIKRAM NATH<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, SANDEEP MEHTA</strong><br> Issue for Consideration The High Court, in a revision filed at the instance of the respondent no.2-complainant, set aside the order granting bail to the accused- appellant herein in a case involving offences triable by the Court of Magistrate after a gap of nearly 8 years. Headnotes&dagger; Code s.437 &ndash; Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 &ndash; s.480 &ndash; Bail &ndash; Grant of &ndash; The dispute between the appellant and respondent no.2-complainant was regarding tenancy rights over a portion of a building &ndash; Respondent no.2-complainant instituted a civil suit<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 09-04-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 1836/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('3','2026','2026_5_221_237','2026INSC367','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='co